    "body": "We've also observed this behaviour occurring in browsers, specifically relating to the 'special case' where `#` and `#top` indicate the 'top of the document'.\r\n\r\nThe [algorithm for scrolling to the fragment](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#scroll-to-the-fragment-identifier) treats 'the top of the document' as a special case (step 2) where the target element is set to null, and the beginning of the document is scrolled to, but unlike the other cases the sequential focus navigation starting point is unchanged.\r\n\r\nWe think this is surprising and undesirable behaviour, and _potentially_ a failure of [WCAG 2.1 2.4.3 Focus Order](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG21/#focus-order) too?\r\n\r\nAgree that adding additional steps to move the keyboard focus / sequential focus navigation starting point when the the indicated part of the document is the top of the document would resolve the issue.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
