    "created_at": "2025-10-28T18:30:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-28T18:30:33Z",
    "body": "It seems @LJWatson may have approached the issue from a different angle. From what I can tell, the relevant part of the spec is actually section [2, not 3](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#scroll-to-the-fragment-identifier).\n\nAt this point, it might be helpful to add a note to [MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/a#linking_to_an_element_on_the_same_page) about the behavior of `href=\"#\"` and `href=\"#top\"` to clarify that keyboard focus does not return to the start of the document, but instead remains on the anchor.\n\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
