    "created_at": "2025-10-30T23:38:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-30T23:38:48Z",
    "body": "> Seems like the proposed text would reset focus to whatever the document's first focusable thing would be, rather than the next focusable element relative to where the target anchor was. It could also direct a screen reader past the intended anchor point, causing users to miss information in between.\n\nI'm not sure that's the effect of the proposed text. If it is, though, it's definitely a problem. I agree we should set sequential focus navigation. It's also okay to reset the focus to the document. However, focusing anything else will cause problems for screen readers, since focus overrides the scroll target location, which might cause a screen reader user to miss content between the scroll target location and whatever got focus.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
